# Predictive Content Auditing & Triage Agent 🚀

**Live Deployed Research Paper:** [https://maazkhan53.github.io/ML-01-Run-the-Starter-Notebooks/](https://maazkhan53.github.io/ML-01-Run-the-Starter-Notebooks/)  
**Author Portfolio:** [https://maazkhan--portfolio.vercel.app/](https://maazkhan--portfolio.vercel.app/)

## What It Does and For Whom
This repository houses the **Predictive Content Auditing Agent**, a machine learning prioritization pipeline built for editorial and technical SEO teams. Managing 30,000+ URLs under finite human bandwidth makes manual portfolio audits impossible. Our framework scores organic decay risk and combines it with 90-day search visibility to route pages into a four-archetype operational Action Playbook.

## Data Provenance & Leakage Prevention
* **Data Provenance:** All results in this repository are **measured and computed directly** on the official FlyRank ML Internship anonymized production dataset (`data/raw/content_refresh_anonymized.csv`), comprising **30,000 production URLs across 32 enterprise client domains** sampled from FlyRank's 79M-row search warehouse.
* **Deliberate Exclusions (13 Columns Purged):** We programmatically exclude direct label derivatives (`trend_direction`, `trend_pct`, `trend_outcome`), entity/pipeline identifiers (`client_id`, `content_id`, `provider_used`, `model_used`), and short-window differential fields (`impressions_last_30d`, `impressions_prev_30d`, `clicks_last_30d`, `clicks_prev_30d`, `sessions_last_30d`, `sessions_prev_30d`) that mechanically leak the target formula.
* **Public-Safety Guarantee:** All entity identifiers are cryptographically hashed; zero client names, domains, or raw URLs exist in the codebase or outputs.

## Validation Architecture & Measured Results (7 Unseen Clients)
We enforce a strict client-grouped holdout split via `GroupShuffleSplit` (`test_size=0.20, random_state=42` on `client_id`): **23,837 training pages across 25 clients** and **6,163 held-out test pages across 7 unseen clients** (0 client overlap).

| Metric / Cutoff | Calibrated Logistic Regression | Week-4 Heuristic Baseline | Held-Out Base Rate | Lift Over Baseline |
| :--- | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: |
| **Precision@10** | **70.0%** (7/10) | 20.0% (2/10) | 51.1% | **+50.0% (3.5×)** |
| **Precision@20** | **60.0%** (12/20) | 40.0% (8/20) | 51.1% | **+20.0% (1.5×)** |
| **Precision@50** | **70.0%** (35/50) | 40.0% (20/50) | 51.1% | **+30.0% (1.75×)** |
| **Held-Out PR-AUC** | **0.5758** | — | 0.5110 | — |
| **Held-Out ROC-AUC** | **0.5821** | — | 0.5000 | — |

* **The Validation Generalization Gap:** Comparing a naive random row split (`0.7197` AP) against our honest client-grouped split (`0.5758` AP) proves that random splitting inflates performance by **+14.4 percentage points** due to cross-row domain memorization.
* **Actionable Triage Queue:** Across all 30,000 pages, **10,670 URLs (35.6%)** are routed into four operational archetypes (*Decaying High-Demand Core*, *Striking-Distance Opportunity*, *High-Visibility CTR Deficit*, and *Thin/Zombie Content*) governed by automated human-review safety guardrails.

## Setup & Reproduction
1. Clone this repository:
   `git clone https://github.com/MaazKhan53/ML-01-Run-the-Starter-Notebooks.git`
2. Install standard dependencies:
   `pip install pandas numpy scikit-learn matplotlib duckdb huggingface_hub`
3. Run `work/notebooks/Solved_capstone.ipynb` (or `work/notebooks/capstone.ipynb`) top-to-bottom (`RANDOM_SEED = 42`).

## Limitations & AI Transparency
* **Observational & Decision-Support Framing:** Predictions capture historical observational associations, not causal refresh proof or search algorithm reverse-engineering.
* **AI Transparency:** Built in collaboration with Gemini and Claude for pipeline scaffolding, type-sanitization debugging, and HTML/SVG presentation, with all validation boundaries (`GroupShuffleSplit` / `GroupKFold`), leakage harness assertions, and metric verifications audited manually.
* **Data Credit:** Built on the FlyRank ML Internship dataset ([https://flyrank.ai](https://flyrank.ai)).
